From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Treggat <taggert2222@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 18:31:54 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 12/27] sycl : split-K small-row MMVQ, gated-delta fusions,
 graph-cache timing

Runtime switches, all default off:
- GGML_SYCL_SMALLROW: split-K MMVQ (one work-group per row, fixed-order
  reduction) for small-row q4_K/q6_K weights at 2..16 columns;
  GGML_SYCL_SMALLROW_MAX_ROWS_Q4K / _Q6K set the row limits
- GGML_SYCL_GDN_FUSE: fuse the gated-delta norm*silu gate and the
  add+softplus+mul alpha chain; with SMALLROW also the ssm_alpha/ssm_beta
  matmuls with their epilogues in one dual split-K launch
  (GGML_SYCL_GDN_FUSE_DUAL=0 disables that part)
- LLAMA_KV_PAD: coarser KV padding (multiple of 256), experimental, untested
GGML_SYCL_GRAPH_STATS now also reports host ms per eager/record/finalize/
replay call. Adds GDN_CHAIN and small-row test-backend-ops cases.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
